.TH SDL_CreateTraySubmenu 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_CreateTraySubmenu \- Create a submenu for a system tray entry.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_tray.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_TrayMenu * SDL_CreateTraySubmenu(SDL_TrayEntry *entry);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This should be called at most once per tray entry\[char46]
.PP
This function does the same thing as
.BR SDL_CreateTrayMenu ,
except that it takes a
.BR SDL_TrayEntry
instead of a
.BR SDL_Tray \[char46]
.PP
A menu does not need to be destroyed; it will be destroyed with the tray\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I entry
the tray entry to bind the menu to\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the newly created menu\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should be called on the thread that created the tray\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_InsertTrayEntryAt (3),
.BR SDL_GetTraySubmenu (3),
.BR SDL_GetTrayMenuParentEntry (3)
